{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1370760-bloodlines-what-is-going-on-in-2e","id":1370760,"title":"Bloodlines-what is going on in 2E?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-27T07:59:33-08:00","id":1370760,"title":"Bloodlines-what is going on in 2E?","content":"reading about the various bloodlines was a guilty pleasure of mine for a while. I will still break out one of the old blood line books and take a read through of some of them. When the 2e came out an all of the splats had there specializations(blood lines,lodges, legacies) neutered/ignored. It was disappointing but if that was the direction the company was taking well okay. At some point in time we go some post on here updating a few blood lines to 2e. <br /> <br /> Then it went dark it was like the company thought blood lines and its like were a non entity. No rules for updating other blood lines, no suggestions on how the creators think blood lines work in the newer setting, until we finally get a book with two new blood lines in it.<br /> <br /> What I don't understand is what is going on from the companies perspective. Blood Lines seemed like a completely dropped priority until that book, can we expect future blood lines maybe up dates.<br /> <br /> Vampire players, at least you guys got an example of a updated blood line, for mage and werewolf players were told go jump off a cliff when it came to rule updates.<br /> <br /> The books just kinda mentioned off handily yeah Legacies and Lodges exist nothing beyond that(at least to my knowledge)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25971-ronstar1981","name":"ronstar1981","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T08:05:43-08:00","id":1370762,"title":"","content":"Uh... Mage gave rules for Legacies, one completed Legacy, another full Legacy in Dark Eras1, characters' attainments whenever a character is statted. Lodges get their rules in the Pack. The latest book for Requiem has some bloodlines in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T08:52:44-08:00","id":1370768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ronstar1981</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1370760-bloodlines-what-is-going-on-in-2e#post1370760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it went dark it was like the company thought blood lines and its like were a non entity. No rules for updating other blood lines, no suggestions on how the creators think blood lines work in the newer setting, until we finally get a book with two new blood lines in it.<br /> <br /> What I don't understand is what is going on from the companies perspective. Blood Lines seemed like a completely dropped priority until that book, can we expect future blood lines maybe up dates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Morbus show up in Dark Eras 1, Khaibit, Neglatu, and Kerberos were released for free on Onyx Path's website, Bron are in Dark Eras 2, and a whole bunch more are in Spilled Blood. Guidelines for making new bloodlines or updating old ones are in Rose's mechanics guide on the ST Vault (&quot;Bloody Dots&quot;).<br /> <br /> I'd also highly recommend Bloodlines: the Devoted (on the ST Vault) for updates of old bloodlines, the writers did an excellent job with it (and some of them also worked on Spilled Blood and/or DE2).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T08:55:39-08:00","id":1370770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ronstar1981</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1370760-bloodlines-what-is-going-on-in-2e#post1370760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire players, at least you guys got an example of a updated blood line, for mage and werewolf players were told go jump off a cliff when it came to rule updates.<br /> <br /> The books just kinda mentioned off handily yeah Legacies and Lodges exist nothing beyond that(at least to my knowledge)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mage core has Legacy creation rules, and I believe there are several Lodges in Shunned by the Moon? They honestly had more support than vampire bloodlines until very recently, bloodline creation rules aren't in the Vampire core at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T09:03:41-08:00","id":1370771,"title":"","content":"The creation rules for vampire bloodlines are simple. Take your favorite clan, give them a fourth previously out of clan discipline and merit chain of alternate powers you want them to be able to do with their disciplines to nullify a drawback or limitation on their disciplines and/or a few vampire abilities without creating devotions and concoct some pulp fiction type background to explain why they have additional powers.<br /> You don't need an entire book telling you how to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-27-2020, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T09:10:51-08:00","id":1370773,"title":"","content":"I own the &quot;The Pack&quot; but never read through it, it just never caught my attention very well. Werewolf is the one game line I have the most experience in as a player but for some reason I could never get into &quot;The Pack&quot;. I guess I let that blind me to the fact the creation rules for Lodges were in the book. <br /> <br /> When it comes to mechanics, I think that is a personal weakness of mine when it comes to designing them with a fair perspective(I.E. not creating broken crap unintended) I look for official sources as a guide line and for awhile I wasn't seeing much. Guess I missed it when it was presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25971-ronstar1981","name":"ronstar1981","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T20:08:45-08:00","id":1372608,"title":"","content":"Must admit i have yet to tackle 2e fully, what to say of bloodline creation rules. It all seems curious, but the combo of laziness to learn a new edition and group breaking around the late run of 1e have a quite strong pull, i guess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T08:38:01-08:00","id":1372717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1370760-bloodlines-what-is-going-on-in-2e?p=1370768#post1370768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Khaibit, Neglatu, and Kerberos were released for free on Onyx Path's website,</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I missed this!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T15:44:52-07:00","id":1374244,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there are examples of how to do these things in the current edition, so you can make an infinite number of bloodlines yourself. What they\u2019re not doing is releasing a bunch of products that only contain bloodlines, as they did in the last edition. Which is understandable because 1) while the odd bloodline in a product is a welcome treat, bloodlines are hit-and-miss in general, in terms of usefulness, and 2) making them is dead simple, so it in many cases it\u2019s probably easier to do it yourself than adapt what someone else has created to suit your needs.<br /> <br /> An extra favored discipline plus an extra bane and you\u2019re pretty much there. Bloodline-specific devotions and merits and blood sorcery are optional bonuses. Then give them some cool, intriguing fluff, and you\u2019re done.<br /> <br /> The main difference in 2e is that there\u2019s less of a push to give every bloodline a unique discipline, as that can get out of hand fast, and a lot of that stuff can be covered with existing disciplines, devotions, and blood sorcery. It\u2019s still an option, just not the first resort.<br /> <br /> Of course, now that I say this, I\u2019m tempted to create a bunch of community content bloodlines. Maybe when I have the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}